Mavergreen/clang-22

This repository builds and republishes a Clang/LLVM toolchain for Mavericks.
It ships three artifacts, built from the same source:

1. mavericks-clang-22-cross-*.pkg (installs into /usr/local/mavergreen/clang22-cross)
   A clang/LLVM toolchain that RUNS on modern Apple-Silicon macOS and TARGETS
   Mac OS X 10.9 (x86_64) out of the box. Built from source from the pinned
   llvm/llvm-project release tarball (see UPSTREAM_VERSION), which is
   GPG-verified against the vendored LLVM release-signer key. Licensed
   Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception.
   Upstream: https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project

2. mavericks-clang-22-native-*.pkg (installs into /usr/local/mavergreen/clang22)
   The same toolchain, RUNNING on Mac OS X 10.9 (x86_64) itself.

3. libcxx22-*.pkg (installs into /usr/local/mavergreen/libcxx22)
   LLVM's libc++ and libc++abi from the same build, as runtime dylibs for
   Mac OS X 10.9 (x86_64). Licensed Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception. Recaulk
   (below) is linked in, not exported.

Each toolchain .pkg also bakes in Recaulk (librecaulk.a plus its wrapper
headers), which back-fills newer-than-10.9 libc/libSystem APIs so a 10.9-targeted
binary links. It is consumed as a prebuilt artifact from Mavergreen/recaulk
(https://github.com/Mavergreen/recaulk); its own back-fills are ISC. The
macports-legacy-support code it builds in
(https://github.com/macports/macports-legacy-support) keeps its own license,
BSD-3-Clause. The pin lives in components/recaulk/version; see INGREDIENTS.md.

The Apple MacOSX10.9 SDK is NOT redistributed here. It is fetched at build
time (and, for an installed toolchain, at first use) by mavericks-shipyard's
fetch_sdk.sh, and remains subject to Apple's own license.

native-bootstrap/ contains Wowfunhappy's original on-10.9 bootstrap scripts
(build.sh, make.sh, lldb.sh, debugserver-shim.py), preserved for a future
local-Mavericks build phase, changed only by the host declaration on each one's
second line. They are not used by CI.
